course: dictionary
lesson: 12628
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word dismissed is a good example. «Class dismissed!» means the teacher lets the pupils leave, but «The boss dismissed Sam for being late» means Sam lost his job.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The idea was dismissed in seconds» means people decided it was not worth thinking about. Ask: what is happening here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In cricket, «The batter was dismissed after scoring 12 runs» means the batter is out. It is the same word with a different meaning, and the clues around it show you which one to choose.
fact: Dismissed is the past form of the verb dismiss.
fact: «Class dismissed!» means the pupils may leave.
fact: «He was dismissed from his job» means he was sacked, or told to leave his job.
fact: «The idea was dismissed» means people decided it was not worth thinking about.
fact: In a law court, a case that is dismissed is ended without going further. In cricket, a dismissed batter is out.
exercise: «Class dismissed!» said Miss Patel, and everyone jumped up. What does dismissed mean here? | The pupils have won a prize | The pupils must sit down and be quiet | *The pupils may leave | The pupils are sacked
exercise: «Ravi was dismissed from his job at the shop.» What does dismissed mean? | The shop gave Ravi a promotion | He was asked to stay late | He went on holiday | *He was sacked and told to leave his job
exercise: «Her idea was dismissed in seconds, and nobody talked about it again.» What does dismissed suggest? | *People decided the idea was not worth thinking about | People asked for more time to think | People wrote the idea down in a book | People loved the idea and voted for it
test: «The batter was dismissed after scoring 12 runs.» In cricket, what does dismissed mean? | The batter scored a century | *The batter was out | The batter had to go home early | The batter was given a second chance
test: Ben says, «The judge dismissed the case, so it is over.» What happened to the case? | It was given to a new judge | It was delayed until next year | It was moved to a bigger court | *It was ended and not taken any further
exam: Mia reads, «The teacher dismissed the class, then dismissed a silly idea.» Which two meanings does dismissed have here? | Let the class stay, and asked the idea to leave | Sacked the class and gave the idea a prize | Sang the class a song and wrote the idea down | *Let the class leave, and decided the idea was not worth thinking about
